      "language": "en",
      "scope": "verified_requested_taxon",
      "clean": "{{Use dmy dates|cs1-dates=ly|date=January 2023}}\n\nHeptapleurum heptaphyllum is a species of flowering plant in the family Araliaceae, native to southern China, Indo-China and Japan. It was first described by Carl Linnaeus in 1771 as Vitis heptaphylla.\n\nSchefflera rubriflora was assessed as \"critically endangered\" in the 2004 IUCN Red List, where it was considered endemic to Yunnan in China, but {{As of|2023|January|lc=yes}} was treated as part of the much more widely distributed Heptapleurum heptaphyllum.",
